The stuffy softboard cubicles inside where we made our stop motion films.

![](@assets/images/posts/gung-ho/ga-2.jpg)

The relatively colder working space at Echostream, Gangtok where we would push around keyframes and flat plastic characters.

![](@assets/images/posts/gung-ho/ga3.jpg)

One of the many sources of warmth, Deergha (in watercolor).

![](@assets/images/posts/gung-ho/ga4.jpg)

A few other daily faces, Akshay, Ranveer, Chewang Rinchen, Tenzing.

![](@assets/images/posts/gung-ho/ga5.jpg)

![](@assets/images/posts/gung-ho/ga6.jpg)

A surprisingly art nouveau-ish street lamp at Upper Syari, where we stayed and a faded mass of ferns and moss on the wall opposite to Pretaste where many warm meals were savoured.

![](@assets/images/posts/gung-ho/ga7.jpg)

I’m assuming this bench has either been repaired and repurposed inside the office or it has ebbed away into the ground which would relieve it of its duties of supporting puffy bottoms on break.

![](@assets/images/posts/gung-ho/ga8.jpg)
